# Keep the production image lean. Multi-stage Dockerfile compiles
# Go + builds the dashboard, then copies only the resulting binary
# into a distroless runtime — but the build context is still the
# whole repo by default, which slows COPY and balloons builder
# image cache. Excluding everything below cuts the build context
# from ~600MB to <20MB on a clean checkout.

# Node ecosystem (workspace-app + dashboard build their own outputs)
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/.cache
**/.parcel-cache
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/.vite

# Go build outputs
**/*.test
**/*.out
**/coverage.out
**/coverage.html
**/bin

# Editor + OS noise
**/.DS_Store
**/.idea
**/.vscode
**/*.swp
**/*.swo

# Version control + CI
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Local env + secrets — defense in depth even though .env should
# never be in the repo to begin with.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Docs + planning artifacts (the dashboard embeds its own runtime
# docs at /docs via go:embed; .work/ is local notes only).
.work
docs
**/*.md
!README.md

# Test fixtures + E2E artifacts
**/testdata
**/__tests__
**/__fixtures__
**/e2e
**/playwright-report
**/playwright/.cache

# Misc
**/.eslintcache
**/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
